  "about": "I'm a Senior Staff Software Engineer and manager at Google who has spent the past 15+ years working at the intersection of machine learning, speech, and AI. I have deep experience leading teams to build and launch new technologies that change how millions of people interact with their devices. My expertise ranges from on-device AI and large language models to speaker recognition and full-stack product quality.\n\nMy career started with academic research in speaker and language recognition at the Universidad Autónoma de Madrid. This foundation led me to Google, where I have spent nearly 15 years developing cutting-edge technology (>9K citations) and products, such as “Hey Google,” VoiceMatch, and the Multilingual Assistant. Since joining Google DeepMind, I have helped shape the future of AI by developing new agents and tools, including Google Home and Workspace Extensions in the Gemini app.\n\nA list of my academic publications is available here: https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TsfUc3cAAAAJ&hl=en",
